{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Be fruitful and multiply.</b> It was necessary to say this to them, for although He said to them when they came out, ״Go out… you and your wife״ etc. (Genesis 8:16), that was merely permission and not a commandment. And the commandment to be fruitful and multiply came here from the Creator. And one must set one's mind to why He repeated a second time to command, saying shortly afterward, ״And you, be fruitful and multiply״ (Genesis 9:7), and was not satisfied with one time. And it appears that one verse comes as a commandment and the second verse comes as an obligation." "And examine precisely His saying <b>and you</b> with the added vav — to say, to the side [i.e., to the effect] that I have sworn to you that no more shall all flesh be cut off, you too must undertake to be fruitful and multiply. And from this point on it is a condition. And accordingly, the statement of our Sages, of blessed memory (Niddah 13a), is precisely understood, for they said: whoever holds the member and urinates is as though he brings a flood upon the world — end quote. Meaning, since the oath of HaShem that [all flesh] shall not be cut off etc. was on the condition that they undertake to be fruitful etc. — accordingly, one who destroys his seed has nullified the condition, and it is as though he brings a flood etc. And understand:"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:17.380035578Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}